hadiths[156]{hadithnumber,text}:
"809","Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Alternate between Hajj and Umrah; for those two remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes filth from iron"""
"810","Abu Hurairah narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever performs Hajj for Allah"""
"811","Ali narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever has the provisions and the means to convey him to Allah's House and he does not perform Hajj"""
"812","Ibn Umar narrated:\A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is it that makes Hajj obligatory?' He said: \""The provisions and a means of conveyance"""
"813","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:\When Allah revealed: And Hajj to the House is a duty that mankind owes to Allah"""
"814","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\The Prophet performed Hajj three times. He performed Hajj twice before his emigration"""
"815","Sa'eed bin Abi Sa'eed Al Maqbury narrated:\Abu Shuraih Al-Adawi said tat when Amr bin Sa'eed was sending troops to Makkah he said to him: 'O Amr! Allow me to tell you what the Messenger of Allah said on the day following the Conquest of Makkah. My ears heard it"""
"816","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\When the Prophet wanted to Perform Hajj"""
"817","Ibn Umar narrated:\Al-Baida the one they lie about regarding the Messenger of Allah. By Allah! The Messenger of Allah did not start the Talbiyah except from near the Masjid"""
"818","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet started the Talbiyah after the Salat"""
"819","Aishah narrated:\the Messenger of Allah performed the Ifrad form of Hajj"""
"820","Anas narrated:\I heard the Prophet saying: (Labbaika Bi'umratin wa Hajjah) 'Here I am for 'Umrah and Hajj"""
"821","Anas narrated:\I heard the Prophet saying: (Labbaika Bi'umratin wa Hajjah) 'Here I am for 'Umrah and Hajj.'\"""""
"822","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal narrated that:He heard Sa'd bin Abi Waqas"
"823","Salim bin Abdullah narrated that :he had heard a man from Ash-Sham asking Abdullah bin Umar about Tamattu after Umrah until Hajj"
"824","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet would say the following for the Talbiyah: \""Labbaik Allahumma labbaik. Labbaik la sharika laka labbaik. Innal-hamda wan-ni;mata laka wal-mulk"""
"825","Nafi` narrated:When Ibn Umar would say the talbiyah he would continue saying: \Labbaik Allahumma labbaik. Labbaik la sharika laka labbaik. Innal-hamda wan-ni`mata laka wal-mulk"""
"826","Abu Bakr As-Siddiq narrated that:The Messenger of Allah was asked: \Which Hajj is the most virtuous?\"" He said: \""That with raised voices (Al-Ajj) and the flow of blood (of the sacrifice) (Ath-Thajj)"""
"827","Sahl bin Sa'd narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \There is no Muslim who says the Talbiyah except that - on his right and left"""
"828","Khallad bin As-Sa'ib (bin Khalad) narrated from his father:Who said that the Messenger of Allah said: \Jibril came to me and ordered me to order my Companions to raise their voices with the Ihlal"""
"829","Zaid bin Thabit narrated from his father :who said that he saw the Prophet disrobing for his Ihlal and to perform Ghusl"
"830","Ibn Umar narrated that:A man said: \Where should we begin our Hil (Ihram) O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""The people of Al-Madinah begin their Hil (Ihram) from Dhul-Hulaifah"""
"831","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet made Al-Aqiq the Miqat for the people of the west"""
"832","Ibn Umar narrated:\A man stood and said 'O Messenger of Allah! What clothing do you command us to wear in Al-Haram?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Do not wear shirts"""
"833","Ibn Abbas narrated that:He heard the Messenger of Allah say: \If the Muhrim cannot find an Izar"""
"834","Ya'la bin Umayyah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah saw a Bedouin who was in Ihram wearing a cloak. So he ordered him to remove it"""
"835","Ya'la bin Umayyah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah saw a Bedouin who was in Ihram wearing a cloak. So he ordered him to remove it"
"836","Aishah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: \Five are Fawasiq which may be killed in the Haram: the mouse"""
"837","Abu Sa'eed narrated that:The Prophet said: \The Muhrim may kill the wild beast of prey"""
"838","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah was cupped while he was a Muhrim"""
"839","Nubaih bin Wahb narrated:\Ibn Ma'mar wanted to have his son married. S he sent me to Aban bin Uthman who was the Amir of the (Hajj) season. I went to him and said: 'Your brother wants to marry his son and he would like for you to witness that.' He said: 'I think he is but a crude Bedouin; indeed the Muhrim is not to marry nor have someone married'\"" - or he said similarly - then he narrated from Uthman similar in Marfu form (from the Prophet)"""
"840","Abu Rafi narrated:\The Messenger of Allah married Maimunah while he was Halal"""
"841","Abu Rafi narrated:""The Messenger of Allah married Maimunah while he was Halal, and he stayed with her while he was Halal, and I was the messenger between the two of them"
"842","(Another chain) that Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet married Maimunah while he was a Muhrim"""
"843","(Another chain) that Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet married Maimunah while he was a Muhrim"""
"844","Yazid bin Al-Asamm narrated about Maimunah:\The Messenger of Allah married he while he was Halal and he stayed with her while he was Halal. She died in Sarif"""
"845","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:The Prophet said: \The land game is lawful for you while you are in Ihram as long as you did not hunt it - or - it was not hunted for you"""
"846","Abu Qatadah narrated that:He was with the Prophet and when he got to one of the roads of Makkah some of the companions were Muhrim and he (Abu Qatadah) was not a Muhrim. So he saw a wild donkey"
"847","Abu Qatadah narrated that:He was with the Prophet and when he got to one of the roads of Makkah some of the companions were Muhrim and he (Abu Qatadah) was not a Muhrim. So he saw a wild donkey, so he mounted his horse, asked his companions to give him his whip but they refused, so he asked them to give him his spear and they refused. So he (himself) took it and struck the donkey killing it. Some of the Companions of the Prophet ate it and some of them refused. When they caught up to the Prophet they asked him about that and he said: ""It is only food which Allah fed you"
"848","Ibn Abbas narrated that:As-S'ab bin Jath-thamah informed him that the Messenger of Allah had passed him at Al-Abwa or Bawaddan. He (As-S'ab) gave him a wild donkey but he refused it. When the Messenger of Allah noticed on his face that he was upset"
"849","Abu Hurairah narrated:\We went with the Messenger of Allah during Hajj or Umrah and we encountered a swarm of locusts. We began striking at them with our whips and set our staffs"""
"850","Ibn Abi Ammar said:\I asked Jabir bin Abdullah: 'Is the hyena game?' He said: 'Yes'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Can it be eaten?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Did the Messenger of Allah say that?' He said: 'Yes"""
"851","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet performed Ghusl for entered Makkah at Fakhkh"""
"852","Aishah narrated:\When Prophet came to Makkah he entered it from its higher side"""
"853","Aishah narrated:""When Prophet came to Makkah he entered it from its higher side, and left from its lower side"
"854","Al-Muhajir Al-Makki said:Jabir bin Abdulla was asked about a man raising his hands when he sees the House (Ka'bah). So he said: 'We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah and we did it"
"855","Yūsuf ibn ‘Īsā narrated to us: Wakī‘ narrated to us: al-‘Umarī narrated from Nāfi‘ from Ibn ‘Umar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) entered Makkah during the daytime.\n\nAbū ‘Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth."
"856","Jabir narrated:\The Prophet performed Raml from the (Black) Stone to the (Black) Stone for three (circuits)"""
"857","**Narration Chain:**\n\nJābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported:\n\n> When the Prophet of Allāh ﷺ arrived in Makkah, he entered the Sacred Mosque and touched the Black Stone (istalām). Then he proceeded to his right and performed ramal (brisk walking) for three circuits, and walked ordinarily for four circuits. Thereafter he came to the Station of Ibrāhīm (maqām) and recited: **\And take the Station of Ibrāhīm as a place of prayer\""** (Sūrah al-Baqarah"
"858","Ibn Ya'la narrated from his father:\The Prophet performed Tawaf of the House Mudtabi'an"""
"859","Abbas bin Rabi'ah said:\I saw Umar bin Al-Khattab kissing the (Black) Stone and saying: 'I am kissing you while I know that you are just a stone"""
"860","Az-Zubair bin Arabi narrated:That a man asked Ibn Umar about touching the (Black) Stone"
"861","**Hannād narrated to us, Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm, from 'Ābis ibn Rabī'ah, who said:**\n\n\I saw 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — kissing the Black Stone (al-Ḥajar al-Aswad) and saying: 'Indeed"
"862","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah only performed the Sa'i of the House and of As-Safa and Al-Marwah to show his strength to the idolaters"""
"863","Kathir bin Jumhan said:\I saw Ibn Umar walking at the place of Sa'i so I said to him: 'Do you walk at the place of Sa'i between As-Safa and Al-Marwah?' He said: 'If I performed Sa'i"""
"864","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet performed Tawaf upon his mount"""
"865","Ibn Abbas narrated:\Whoever performed Tawaf around the House fifty time"""
"866","Ayyub As-Sakhtiyani said:\We considered Abdullah bin Sa'eed bin Jubair to be better than his father"""
"867","Jubair bin Mut'im narrated that :the Prophet said: \O Banu Abd Manaf! Do not prevent anyone from performing Tawaf around this House"""
"868","**Narrated to us Ibn Abī ʿUmar, narrated to us Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyyānī, who said:**\n\n\They used to consider ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr to be more excellent than his father.\""\n\n\""And ʿAbdullāh had a brother whose name was ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"
"869","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father:that he considered it recommended for the two Rak'ah of Tawaf to recite: Say: \O you disbelievers!\"" and: Say: \""He is Allah"""
"870","Zaid bin Uthai said:XI asked Ali: \What is it that you were sent with?\"" He said: \""With four things: None will be admitted into Paradise except for the soul that is a Muslim. None is to perform Tawaf around the House while naked. The Muslims and the idolaters will not be gathering (in Makkah) together after this year. And for whomever there is a covenant between him and the Prophet"""
"871","Zaid bin Uthai said:(Another chain) and they said: \Zaid bin Yuthai\"" and this is more correct"""
"872","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet left me while he had a joyous look of contentment and he returned to me grieving. So I asked him about that and he said: 'I entered the Ka'bah"""
"873","Ibn Umar narrated from Bilal:\The Prophet performed Salat in the interior of the Ka'bah.\"" And Ibn Abbas said: \""He did not perform Salat in it"""
"874","Al-Aswad bin Yazid narrated that:Ibn Az-Zubair said to him: \Narrated to me from what the Mother of the Believers used to (secretly) inform you about\"" - meaning Aishah - so he said: \""She narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Had your people not been still close to the pre-Islamic period of ignorance"""
"875","Al-Aswad bin Yazid narrated that:Ibn Az-Zubair said to him: ""Narrated to me from what the Mother of the Believers used to (secretly) inform you about"" - meaning Aishah - so he said: ""She narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Had your people not been still close to the pre-Islamic period of ignorance, then I would demolish the Ka'bah and rebuild it with two doors.'"" He said: ""So when Ibn Az-Zubair came to power he demolished it and rebuilt it with two doors"
"876","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \The Black Stone descended from the Paradise"""
"877","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that :He heard the Messenger of Allah saying: \Indeed the Corner and the Maqam are two corundums from the corundum of Paradise. Allah removed their lights"""
"878","Ata reported that Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah led us in Salat at Mina for Zuhr"""
"879","Narrated Qutaybah, narrated Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ, from Rajāʾ Abū Yaḥyā, who said: I heard Musāfiʿ al-Ḥājib say: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say:\n\n\Indeed"
"880","Aishah said:\We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Shall we build a structure to shade you at Mina? He said: 'No."""
"881","Harithah bin Wahb said:\I prayed two Rak'ah with the Prophet at Mina"""
"882","Yūsuf ibn ‘Īsā and Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated to us, both saying: Wakī‘ narrated to us, from Isrā’īl, from Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir, from Yūsuf ibn Māhak, from his mother, Musaykah, from ‘Ā’ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), who said:\n\nWe said: “O Messenger of Allāh ﷺ, shall we not build for you a structure to provide shade for you at Minā?”\n\nHe ﷺ replied: “No. Minā is the halting place of whoever arrives first.”\n\nAbū ‘Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth."
"883","Aishah narrated:\The Quraish and those who followed their religion - and they were called Al-Hums - would stand at Al-Muzdalifah"""
"884","**Qutaybah narrated to us:** Sufyan ibn 'Uyunah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Yazid ibn Shayban, who said:\n\n**\Ibn Murba' al-Ansari came to us while we were standing at the station (al-Mawqif) at a place that 'Amr would keep at a distance from. He said: 'Indeed"
"885","Jabir narrated:\The Prophet hurried through Wadi Muhassir.\"" Bishr (one of the narrators) added: \""He departed from Jam calmly and he ordered them (the people) to be calm.\"" And Abu Nu'aim (one of the narrators) added: \""And he ordered them to do the stoning with what was similar to pebbles for Al-Khadhf' And he said: \""Perhaps I will not see you after this year"""
"886","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn ‘Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi‘ah; from Zayd ibn ‘Ali; from his father; from ‘Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi‘; from ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood at ‘Arafah and said: ""This is ‘Arafah, and this is the standing place (al-mawqif), and all of ‘Arafah is a standing place."" Then he departed when the sun had set, and he seated Usamah ibn Zayd behind him, and he gestured with his hand in his posture, while the people were striking right and left; he turned to them and said: ""O people, (maintain) tranquility!"" Then he came to Muzdalifah and prayed the two prayers (Maghrib and ‘Isha) together there. When morning came, he came to Quzah, stood upon it, and said: ""This is Quzah, and it is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifah is a standing place."" Then he departed until he reached Wadi Muhassir; he urged his she-camel and she hurried until she crossed the valley. Then he stopped and seated al-Fadl behind him. Then he came to the Jamrah and stoned it. Then he came to the slaughtering place (al-Manhar) and said: ""This is the slaughtering place, and all of Mina is a slaughtering place."" A young woman from Khath‘am asked him for a ruling; she said: ""My father is an old man who has become unable to perform the obligation of Hajj; will it suffice if I perform Hajj on his behalf?"" He said: ""Perform Hajj on behalf of your father."" He turned the neck of al-Fadl (away from her). Al-‘Abbas said: ""O Messenger of Allah, why did you turn the neck of your cousin?"" He said: ""I saw a young man and a young woman, and I did not trust Satan with them."" Then a man came to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I departed (from Muzdalifah) before I shaved (my head)."" He said: ""Shave or shorten (your hair), and there is no sin."" Then another came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I stoned."" He said: ""Stone, and there is no sin."" Then he came to the House (Ka‘bah) and circumambulated it. Then he came to Zamzam and said: ""O Banu ‘Abd al-Muttalib, were it not that people would crowd you out of it, I would have drawn (water)."" In this chapter there is a narration from Jabir. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of ‘Ali is Hasan Sahih; we do not know it from the hadith of ‘Ali except through this route, from the hadith of ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn ‘Ayyash. And more than one narrated it from al-Thawri similarly. The practice upon this among the people of knowledge: they saw that Zuhr and ‘Asr should be combined at ‘Arafah in the time of Zuhr. And some people of knowledge said: If a man prays in his camp and does not witness the prayer with the Imam, if he wishes he may combine the two prayers just as the Imam did. He said: And Zayd ibn ‘Ali is the son of Husayn ibn ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib, upon him be peace."
"887","(Another chain) that Sa'eed bin Jubair narrated :Similarly from Ibn Umar"
"888","Abdur-Rahman bin Ya'mar narrated that:Some people among the residents of Najd came to the Messenger of Allah while he was at Arafat. They were questioning him"
"889","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa‘id narrated to us; from Isma‘il ibn Abi Khalid; from Abu Ishaq; from Sa‘id ibn Jubayr; from Ibn ‘Umar; from the Prophet (ﷺ) with the like of it. Muhammad ibn Bashshar said: Yahya said: The correct version is the hadith of Sufyan. He said: In this chapter there are narrations from ‘Ali, Abu Ayyub, ‘Abdullah ibn Mas‘ud, Jabir, and Usamah ibn Zayd. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Ibn ‘Umar in the narration of Sufyan is more authentic than the narration of Isma‘il ibn Abi Khalid, and the hadith of Sufyan is Sahih Hasan. Abu ‘Isa said: And Isra’il narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq from ‘Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn ‘Umar. And the hadith of Sa‘id ibn Jubayr from Ibn ‘Umar is also Hasan Sahih; Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Sa‘id ibn Jubayr. As for Abu Ishaq, he narrated it from ‘Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn ‘Umar. The practice upon this among the people of knowledge is because Maghrib prayer is not prayed without combining; so when one comes to Jam‘ (Muzdalifah), he combines the two prayers with one Iqamah and does not pray voluntary prayers between them. This is what some people of knowledge chose and followed. And it is the saying of Sufyan al-Thawri. Sufyan said: And if he wishes, he may pray Maghrib, then dine, then put down his garments, then establish (Iqamah) and pray ‘Isha. And some people of knowledge said: He combines Maghrib and ‘Isha at Muzdalifah with one Adhan and two Iqamahs: he gives Adhan for Maghrib, establishes and prays Maghrib, then establishes and prays ‘Isha. This is the saying of al-Shafi‘i. Abu ‘Isa said: And Isra’il narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq from ‘Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn ‘Umar. And the hadith of Sa‘id ibn Jubayr from Ibn ‘Umar is also Hasan Sahih; Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated it from Sa‘id ibn Jubayr. And as for Abu Ishaq, he narrated it from ‘Abdullah and Khalid, the two sons of Malik, from Ibn ‘Umar."
"890","Urwah bin Mudarris bin Aws bin Harithah bin Lam At-Ta'i narrated:\I came to the Messenger of Allah at Al-Muzdalifah when he left for the Salat. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I came from the two mountains of (the tribe of) Tai"""
"891","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah sent me with the Thaqal (load of baggage) during the night from Jam"""
"892","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet advanced the weak among his family and he said: 'Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun has risen"""
"893","Jabir narrated:\The Prophet would stone on the Day of An-Nahr during the morning light"""
"894","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Waki‘ narrated to us; from al-Mas‘udi; from al-Hakam; from Miqsam; from Ibn ‘Abbas, that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent ahead the weak members of his family and said: ""Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises."" Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Ibn ‘Abbas is Hasan Sahih. The practice upon this hadith among the people of knowledge: they did not see any harm in the weak departing from Muzdalifah at night, proceeding to Mina. And most of the people of knowledge, based on the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ), said that they do not stone until the sun rises. And some people of knowledge granted a concession to stone at night. The practice is upon the hadith of the Prophet (ﷺ) that they do not stone. And this is the saying of al-Thawri and al-Shafi‘i. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Ibn ‘Abbas: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me in a group (thaqal)"" is a Sahih hadith, narrated from him through other routes. And Shu‘bah narrated this hadith from Mushash from ‘Ata’ from Ibn ‘Abbas from al-Fadl ibn ‘Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent ahead the weak members of his family from Jam‘ at night. This hadith is an error; Mushash erred in it and added al-Fadl ibn ‘Abbas. And Ibn Jurayj and others narrated this hadith from ‘Ata’ from Ibn ‘Abbas, and they did not mention al-Fadl ibn ‘Abbas in it. And Mushash is a Basri; Shu‘bah narrated from him."
"895","Amr bin Maimun narrated:\We were halted at Jama when Umar bin Al-Khattab said: 'The idolaters would not depart until the sun had risen and they would say: \""Let the sun shine on Thabir\"" and indeed the Messenger of Allah contradicted them.' So Umar departed before the rising of the sun"""
"896","Jabir narrated:\I saw the Messenger of Allah stoning the Jimar with what was similar to pebbles for Al-Khadhaf"""
"897","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Messenger of Allah stoned the Jimar when the sun had passed the zenith"""
"898","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet stoned the Jamrah on the Day of An-Nahr while riding"""
"899","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet would walk when stoning the Jimar"""
"900","Ibn Umar narrated:""The Prophet would walk when stoning the Jimar, both going and returning"
"901","Aishah narrated that:The Prophet said: \Stoning the Jimari and Sa'i between As-Safa and Al-Marwah are only done for the establishment of Allah's remembrance"""
"902","Qudamah bin Abdullah said:\I saw the Prophet stoning the Jimar upon his she-camel; there was no hitting"""
"903","Jabir narrated:\We slaughtered with the Messenger of Allah during the year of Al-Hudaibiyah: a cow for seven"""
"904","Ibn Abbas narrated:\We were with the Prophet on a journey (on the Day of) Adha"""
"905","Ibn Abbas narrated:\The Prophet garlanded two sandals and marked the Hadi on the right side at Dhul-Hulaifah"""
"906","**Narrated to us al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth and others, one of them said: Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā, from Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from ʿIlbāʾ ibn Aḥmar, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:**\n\n\We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey"
"907","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Waki‘ narrated to us; from Hisham al-Dastawa’i; from Qatadah; from Abu Hassan al-A‘raj; from Ibn ‘Abbas, that the Prophet (ﷺ) put sandals (qallada na‘layn) on the sacrificial animal and garlanded (ash‘ara) it on the right side at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and he turned away the blood from it. He said: In this chapter there is a narration from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Ibn ‘Abbas is Hasan Sahih. And Abu Hassan al-A‘raj’s name is Muslim. The practice upon this among the people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) and others: they regard garlanding (ish‘ar) as prescribed. And this is the saying of al-Thawri, al-Shafi‘i, Ahmad, and Ishaq. Abu ‘Isa said: I heard Yusuf ibn ‘Isa say: I heard Waki‘ say when he narrated this hadith: ""Do not look at the saying of the people of opinion (Ahl al-Ra’y) in this, for garlanding is a Sunnah, and their saying is an innovation."" He said: And I heard Abu al-Sa’ib say: We were with Waki‘ when he said to a man with him who was of the people of opinion: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) garlanded, and Abu Hanifah says it is mutilation (muthlah)."" The man said: ""But it has been narrated from Ibrahim al-Nakha‘i that he said garlanding is mutilation."" He said: I saw Waki‘ become severely angry and said: ""I tell you the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, and you say Ibrahim said? You most deserve to be imprisoned and not released until you retract this saying of yours."""
"908","Aishah narrated:\I twisted the garlands for all of the Hadi of the Messenger of Allah"""
"909","Najiyah Al-Khuza'i (the Companion of the Messenger of Allah) said:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What should be done with the afflicted among the Hadi?' He said: 'Slaughter them"""
"910","Anas bin Malik narrated:That the Prophet saw a man driving his Badanah so he said to him: \Ride it.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah! It is a Badanah.\"" So on the third or fourth time he said to him: \""Ride it. And woe to you"""
"911","Anas bin Malik narrated:That the Prophet saw a man driving his Badanah so he said to him: ""Ride it."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! It is a Badanah."" So on the third or fourth time he said to him: ""Ride it. And woe to you"
"912","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \May Allah have mercy upon those who shaved\"" saying it one or two times"""
"913","Ali narrated:\The Messenger of Allah prohibited that a woman should shave her head"""
"914","(Another chain) with similar (as no. 914) from Khilas:But he did not mention \from Ali"""
"915","Abdullah bin Amr narrated:\A man asked the Messenger of Allah: 'I shaved before slaughtering.' So he said: 'Slaughter"""
"916","Aishah narrated:\I put perfume with musk in it on the Messenger of Allah before he assumed Ihram"""
"917","Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated:\I was a companion rider with the Messenger of Allah from Jam to Mina. He did not cease saying the Talbiyah until stoning Jamrat Al-Aqabah"""
"918","Ibn Abbas narrated:(that the Prophet): \Would stop saying the Talbiyah during \""Umrah when he touched the (Black) Stone"""
"919","Aishah narrated:\The Prophet delayed the visiting Tawaf until the night"""
"920","**Hannād narrated to us** — Hushaym narrated to us — from Ibn Abī Laylā — from ʿAṭāʾ — from Ibn ʿAbbās, who raised the Hadith to the Prophet ﷺ, that **he would cease uttering the Talbiyah during the ʿUmrah upon touching (or kissing) the Black Stone (al-Ḥajar al-Aswad).**\n\nHe (Abū ʿĪsā) said: **And there are narrations on this subject from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr.**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: **The Hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās is a Ṣaḥīḥ (authentic) Hadith.**\n\n**And the practice (al-ʿamal) according to the majority of the people of knowledge is based upon it.** They said: **\The one performing ʿUmrah does not cease the Talbiyah until he touches (or kisses) the Black Stone.\""**\n\nAnd some of them said: **\""When he reaches the houses of Makkah"
"921","Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who narrated from Sufyān, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet ﷺ delayed the Ṭawāf al-Ziyārah (the circumambulation of visit) until the night.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.\n\nSome scholars have permitted the delay of Ṭawāf al-Ziyārah until the night, while some of them preferred that it be performed on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr). Others have given broader leeway, allowing its delay even until the last days of Minā."
"922","Aishah narrated:\The Messenger of Allah only camped at Al-Abtah because it was easier for his departure"""
"923","Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\A woman held a boy of hers up for the Messenger of Allah and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is there Hajj for this one' He said: 'Yes"""
"924","As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated:\My father took me for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah during the Farewell Hajj"""
"925","**Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrated:**\n\nA woman raised her young child to the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) and said, \O Messenger of Allāh"
"926","Jabir narrated:\When we performed our Hajj with the Prophet we would say the Talbiyah for the women and we would stone for the boys"""
"927","Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated:\A woman from Khath'am said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My father has lived until Allah has made Hajj obligatory"""
"928","Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father who said:\A woman came to the Prophet and said: 'My mother died and she did not perform Hajj should I perform Hajj on her behalf?' He said: 'Yes"""
"929","Abu Razin Al-Uqaili narrated:That he went to the Prophet and said: \O Messenger of Allah! My father is an elderly man who is not able to perform Hajj nor Umrah nor undertake a journey.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah"""
"930","Jabir narrated that:The Prophet was asked about whether Umrah was obligatory? He said: \No. But if you perform Umrah it is more virtuous"""
"931","Ibn Abbas narrated:That the Prophet said: \Umrah has been entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection"""
"932","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\Umrah to 'Umrah atones for the sins between them"""
"933","Amr bin Aws narrated from Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr:\The Prophet ordered Abdur-RAhman bin Abi Bakr to (accompany) Aishah to perform Umrah from At-Tan'im"""
"934","Muharrish Al-Kabi narrated:\The Messenger of Allah left Al-Ji'irranah during the night for Umrah"""
"935","Urwah said:Ibn Umar was asked: In which month did the Messenger of Allah perform Umrah? He said: 'During Rajab.' So Aishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah did not perform Umrah except that he was with him - meaning Ibn Umar - and he did not ever perform Umrah in the month of Rajab"
"936","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshār, narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muzāḥim ibn Abī Muzāḥim, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from al-Muḥarish al-Kaʿbī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from al-Jiʿrānah at night as a *muʿtamir* (one seeking to perform ʿUmrah), and he entered Makkah at night and completed his ʿUmrah. He then departed that same night and rose the following morning at al-Jiʿrānah as though he had spent the night there. When the sun had passed its zenith the next day, he set forth from the valley of Sarif, joining the road to the route of Jamʿ at the valley of Sarif. It is on account of this that his ʿUmrah remained concealed from the people.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: This is a *gharīb* ḥasan hadith. We do not know of any other hadith from al-Muḥarish al-Kaʿbī from the Prophet ﷺ besides this one.\n\n- **al-Jiʿrānah**: A location near Makkah, historically used as a *mīqāt* (station for assuming *iḥrām*).\n- **Muʿtamir**: One performing the ʿUmrah (the lesser pilgrimage).\n- **al-Jiʿrānah**: A place near Makkah where the Prophet ﷺ distributed the war booty of Hunayn before assuming *iḥrām* for ʿUmrah.\n- **Sarif**: A valley located between Makkah and Madinah.\n- **Jamʿ**: A reference to the area of Muzdalifah, where pilgrims gather during the Ḥajj.\n- **Ḥasan gharīb**: A hadith classified as \good\"""""""" (*ḥasan*) and \""""""""rare/singular\"""""""" (*gharīb*)"
"937","Al-Bara narrated:\The Prophet performed Umrah during Dhul-Qa'dah"""
"938","Umm Ma'qil narrated that:The Prophet said: \Umrah during Ramadan is equal to Hajj"""
"939","Ikrimah narrated from Al-Hajjaj bin Amr who narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever suffers a fracture or becomes lame them he (leaves the state of Ihram) and is required to perform another Hajj.\"" I (Ikrimah) mentioned that to Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas and they said: \""He told the truth"""
"940","Ibn Abbas narrated:\Duba'ah bint Az-Zubair came to the prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I want to perform Hajj so should I state a condition?' He said: 'Yes.' She asked: 'So how should I say it?' He said: 'Say; \""Labbaik Allahumma labbaika mahilli minal Ard haithu tahbisuni (I respond to Your call O Allah"""
"941","Salim narrated that :His father disliked making a condition during Hajj and he said: 'Is not the Sunnah of your Prophet enough for you?"
"942","Aishah narrated:\It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah that Safiyyah bint Huyai got her menses during the days of Mina"""
"943","**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani', who narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, who informed me from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to reject the practice of stipulating a condition (al-ishtirat) during Hajj, and he would say: \Is not the Sunnah of your Prophet"
"944","Aishah narrated:\\n\\n I got my menses do the Prophet ordered me to carry out all the rites except for Tawaf around the House. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 945 Arabic Hadees: 945\""945"""
"945","Abu ‘Ammar narrated to us; ‘Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us; from ‘Ubaydullah ibn ‘Umar; from Nafi‘; from Ibn ‘Umar, who said: Whoever performs Hajj to the House, let his last act be (the farewell circumambulation of) the House, except for menstruating women, for whom the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted a concession. Abu ‘Isa said: The hadith of Ibn ‘Umar is Hasan Sahih. The practice upon this is among the people of knowledge."
"946","Jabir narrated:\The Messenger of Allah performed Qaran for Hajj and Umrah"""
"947","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \Whoever assumes Ihram for Hajj and Umrah"""
"948","Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami narrated :(that the Prophet said): \The Muhajir may stay for three (days) in Makkah after carrying out his rites"""
"949","Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami narrated :(that the Prophet said): ""The Muhajir may stay for three (days) in Makkah after carrying out his rites"
"950","Ibn Abbas narrated:\We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey when he saw a man fall from his camel"""
"951","Nubaih bin Wahb narrated that :Umar bin Ubaidullah bin Ma'mar was complaining about his eyes while he was a Muhrim. He asked Aban bin Uthman about it and he said: \Bandage it with some aloes"""
"952","Abdur-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated from Ka'b bin Ujrah that:The Prophet passed by him while he was at Al-Hudaibiyah"
"953","Abi Al-Baddah bin Adi narrated from his father:\The Prophet permitted the shepherds to stone a day and leave a day"""
"954","Abi Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi narrated from his father:\The Messenger of Allah permitted the camel herders who were in the camp (at Mina) to stone on the Day of An-Nahr then to gather the stoning of two days after the Day of An-Nahr"""
"955","Anas bin Malik narrated:\When Ali returned to the Messenger of Allah from Yemen he said: 'For what did you intended the Talbiyah?' He replied: 'I intended the Talbiyah for what the Messenger of Allah announced it.' So he (pbuh) said: 'If I did not have the Hadi with me then I would exit Ihram"""
"956","Ali narrated:\I asked the Messenger of Allah about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar and he said: 'They Day of An-Nahr"""
"957","Ali narrated:""I asked the Messenger of Allah about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar and he said: 'They Day of An-Nahr"
"958","Ibn Ubaid bin Umair narrated from his father:\Ibn Umar was clinging on the two corners (in a manner that I had not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet doing) so I said: 'O Abu Abdur-Rahman! You are clinging on the two corners in a manner that I have not seen any of the Companions of the Prophet clining.' So he said: 'I do it because I heard the Messenger of Allah saying: \""Touching them atones for sins.\"" And I heard him saying: \""Whoever performs Tawaf around this House seven times and he keeps track of it"""
"959","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: \Tawaf around the House is similar to Salat except that you talk during it. So whoever talks in it"""
"960","Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said about the (Black) Stone: \By Allah! Allah will raise it on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes by which it sees and a tongue that it speaks with"""
"961","Ibn Umar narrated:\The Prophet would apply oil that is not scented (Ghair Muqattat) while he was a Muhrim"""
"962","**Qutaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn as-Sa'ib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Abbas رضي الله عنهما, that the Prophet ﷺ said:**\n\n*\Circumambulation (Tawaf) around the House (i.e."
"963","Abdul-Aziz bin Rufai narrated:\I said to Anas bin Malik: 'Narrated something to me that you understand about where the Messenger of Allah performed Zuhr on the Day of Tarwiyah.' He said: 'In Mina.'\"" \""I said: 'So where did he pray Asr on the day of departure?' He said: 'In Al-Abtab.' Then he said: 'Do what your leaders do"""
"964","Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \The believer is not afflicted by the prick of a thorn or what is worse (or greater) than that"""
